ling of weakness or a dragging sensation along with the inability to walk, and if the condition has been progressing or has a history of trauma (even if not directly related to the current acute episode), Causticum could be indicated. The \'few years back\' hip damage history might be relevant here.\",\"matching_symptoms\":[\"inability to walk\",\"paralysis\",\"weakness in lower extremities\",\"history of trauma\"],\"reference\":\"Hahnemann\'s Materia Medica Pura\"},{\"name\":\"Arsenicum album\",\"match_percentage\":65,\"potency\":\"30C\",\"reasoning\":\"While less likely given the lack of other Arsenicum symptoms, if the patient experiences extreme restlessness and anxiety associated with the inability to walk, and a fear of movement due to weakness, Arsenicum could be considered. The \'suddenly occurred\' aspect might fit if it\'s accompanied by a rapid decline in function.\",\"matching_symptoms\":[\"inability to walk\",\"restlessness\",\"anxiety\",\"fear of movement\"],\"reference\":\"Kent\'s Repertory\"},{\"name\":\"Gelsemium sempervirens\",\"match_percentage\":60,\"potency\":\"200C\",\"reasoning\":\"Gelsemium is indicated for weakness and paralysis, particularly in the limbs, often with trembling. If the patient feels heavy and weak in the legs, making it impossible to lift them to walk, and if there\'s a sense of dread or anticipation of bad news (though not explicitly stated, it\'s a common Gelsemium state), it could be a consideration. The \'suddenly occurred\' aspect can also fit Gelsemium.\",\"matching_symptoms\":[\"inability to walk\",\"weakness in legs\",\"trembling\",\"heavy limbs\",\"sudden onset\"],\"reference\":\"Boenninghausen\'s Therapeutic Pocket Book\"}],\"case_analysis\":\"This is a 25-year-old male presenting with a sudden onset of inability to walk for 10 days, with associated knee pain. He reports that both hips were damaged a few years ago, and the current condition occurred suddenly. He is ambithermal, has a normal appetite, and no known al