hus tox. The \'few years back\' history of hip damage could indicate a chronic underlying condition that has acutely flared up. Rhus tox is known for its marked stiffness and pain that is worse from rest and ameliorated by continued motion, which aligns with the inability to take a step.\",\"matching_symptoms\":[\"inability to walk\",\"stiffness\",\"pain worse from rest\",\"sudden onset\",\"hip damage\"],\"reference\":\"Kent\'s Repertory\"},{\"name\":\"Bryonia alba\",\"match_percentage\":80,\"potency\":\"200C\",\"reasoning\":\"While Rhus tox is better from motion, Bryonia is characteristically worse from the slightest motion. The inability to take a step could be due to extreme pain that is aggravated by any movement. The \'suddenly occurred\' aspect can also fit Bryonia if the pain is intense and sharp.\",\"matching_symptoms\":[\"inability to walk\",\"pain worse from slightest motion\",\"sudden onset\"],\"reference\":\"Kent\'s Repertory\"},{\"name\":\"Calcarea carbonica\",\"match_percentage\":75,\"potency\":\"1M\",\"reasoning\":\"Given the history of \'both hip damaged\' occurring \'few years back\', Calcarea carbonica is a strong contender for a deeper constitutional remedy. It is indicated for bone affections, joint pains, and a general feeling of weakness and inability to bear weight, which could manifest as an inability to walk. The slow, gradual development of such a condition often points to Calcarea.\",\"matching_symptoms\":[\"hip damage\",\"inability to walk\",\"weakness\",\"bone affections\",\"joint pains\"],\"reference\":\"Boenninghausen\'s Materia Medica & Repertory\"},{\"name\":\"Apis mellifica\",\"match_percentage\":70,\"potency\":\"30C\",\"reasoning\":\"If there is any underlying inflammation or swelling associated with the knee pain, Apis could be considered. Apis is known for its stinging pains, swelling, and amelioration from cold applications. While not the primary indication for inability to walk, if the knee pain is the primary driver of the imm