, \"right\", \"quadrant\", \"rebound\", \"tender\", \"Fever\", \"Right Lower Quadrant Pain\", \"Nausea\", \"Vomiting\", \"Loss of Appetite\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"CBC showing leukocytosis (WBC >10,000), Elevated CRP, Urinalysis to rule out UTI\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Warning signs present; Consistent clinical findings; Expected findings: McBurney point tenderness, Rovsing sign positive, Psoas sign positive, Obturator sign positive, Guarding, Rebound tenderness\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Mesenteric lymphadenitis, Ovarian cyst rupture, Ectopic pregnancy, UTI, Gastroenteritis, Meckel diverticulum\"}, {\"urgency\": \"routine\", \"category\": \"urological\", \"icd_code\": \"N39.0\", \"severity\": \"mild\", \"diagnosis\": \"Urinary Tract Infection\", \"confidence\": 45, \"typical_onset\": \"acute\", \"confidence_level\": \"Low\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"Watch for: High fever with chills (suggests pyelonephritis), Flank pain, Nausea/vomiting, Altered mental status | Consider tests: Urinalysis (pyuria, bacteriuria, nitrites positive), Urine culture, CBC if systemic | Rule out: Vaginitis, STIs, Interstitial cystitis, Kidney stones, Prostatitis\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"fever\", \"nausea\", \"vomiting\", \"tenderness\", \"tender\", \"Fever\", \"Abdominal Pain\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"Urinalysis (pyuria, bacteriuria, nitrites positive), Urine culture, CBC if systemic\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Warning signs present; Consistent clinical findings; Expected findings: Suprapubic tenderness, Costovertebral angle tenderness (if pyelonephritis), Fever\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Vaginitis, STIs, Interstitial cystitis, Kidney stones, Prostatitis\"}, {\"urgency\": \"urgent\", \"category\": \"infectious\", \"icd_code\": \"A90\", \"severity\": \"moderate\", \"diagnosis\": \"Dengue Fever\", \"confidence\": 43, \"typical_onset\": \"acute\", \"confidence_level\": \"Low\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"⚡ URGENT: Prompt evaluation recommended | Watch for: Severe abdominal pain, Persistent vomiting, Bleeding, Rapid breathing, Restlessness, Fatigue | Consider tests: CBC (thrombocytopenia, leukopenia), Dengue NS1 antigen, Dengue IgM/IgG, LFT, Hematocrit | Rule out: Malaria, Chikungunya, Zika, Typhoid, Leptospirosis\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"fever\", \"abdominal pain\", \"nausea\", \"vomiting\", \"abdominal\", \"High Grade Fever\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"CBC (thrombocytopenia, leukopenia), Dengue NS1 antigen, Dengue IgM/IgG, LFT, Hematocrit\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Warning signs present; Consistent clinical findings; Expected findings: Fever, Rash, Hepatomegaly, Positive tourniquet test, Petechiae\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Malaria, Chikungunya, Zika, Typhoid, Leptospirosis\"}, {\"urgency\": \"urgent\", \"category\": \"respiratory\", \"icd_code\": \"J18\", \"severity\": \"moderate\", \"diagnosis\": \"Community Acquired Pneumonia\", \"confidence\": 37, \"typical_onset\": \"acute\", \"confidence_level\": \"Low\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"⚡ URGENT: Prompt evaluation recommended | Watch for: High fever >39°C, Severe respiratory distress, Cyanosis, Altered consciousness, Blood in sputum | Consider tests: CBC (leukocytosis), CRP elevated, Procalcitonin, Sputum culture, Blood culture, ABG | Rule out: Bronchitis, Tuberculosis, Lung cancer, Pulmonary embolism, Heart failure, COVID-19\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"fever\", \"loss of appetite\", \"loss\", \"appetite\", \"Fever\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"CBC (leukocytosis), CRP elevated, Procalcitonin, Sputum culture, Blood culture, ABG\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Warning signs present; Expected findings: Tachypnea, Decreased breath sounds, Crackles/rales, Bronchial breathing, Dullness to percussion, Increased vocal fremitus\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Bronchitis, Tuberculosis, Lung cancer, Pulmonary embolism, Heart failure, COVID-19\"}, {\"urgency\": \"urgent\", \"category\": \"digestive\", \"icd_code\": \"K81\", \"severity\": \"moderate\", \"diagnosis\": \"Acute Cholecystitis\", \"confidence\": 33, \"typical_onset\": \"acute\", \"confidence_level\": \"Low\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"⚡ URGENT: Prompt evaluation recommended | Watch for: High fever, Severe RUQ pain, Signs of sepsis, Peritonitis | Consider tests: CBC (leukocytosis), LFT (may be elevated), Lipase, CRP | Rule out: Peptic ulcer, Pancreatitis, Hepatitis, Appendicitis, Right lower lobe pneumonia\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"fever\", \"nausea\", \"vomiting\", \"loss of appetite\", \"tenderness\", \"guarding\", \"loss\", \"appetite\", \"right\", \"quadrant\", \"tender\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"CBC (leukocytosis), LFT (may be elevated), Lipase, CRP\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Warning signs present; Consistent clinical findings; Expected findings: RUQ tenderness, Murphy sign positive, Guarding, Palpable gallbladder, Jaundice\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Peptic ulcer, Pancreatitis, Hepatitis, Appendicitis, Right lower lobe pneumonia\"}]','[95, 45, 43, 37, 33]','Based on analysis of symptoms (fever, abdominal pain, right lower quadrant, nausea, vomiting):\n\nPRIMARY CONSIDERATION: Acute Appendicitis (Confidence: High - 95%)\n\nDIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSES TO CONSIDER:\n- Urinary Tract Infection (45%)\n- Dengue Fever (43%)\n\nRECOMMENDED INVESTIGATIONS:\nCBC showing leukocytosis (WBC >10,000), Elevated CRP, Urinalysis to rule out UTI','2025-12-22 08:06:30'),(8,1,NULL,NULL,'increased thirst, frequent urination, fatigue, blurred vision, weight loss','Patient complains of excessive thirst and urination for 2 weeks. Has lost 5kg weight despite eating well. Feeling tired and weak. Dehydrated, dry skin, fruity breath odor','Fasting blood glucose 280 mg/dL, HbA1c 9.5%','[{\"urgency\": \"emergency\", \"category\": \"neurological\", \"icd_code\": \"I63\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"diagnosis\": \"Ischemic Stroke\", \"confidence\": 95, \"typical_onset\": \"sudden\", \"confidence_level\": \"High\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"⚠️ EMERGENCY: Requires immediate attention | Watch for: Complete paralysis, Loss of consciousness, Signs of herniation | Consider tests: CBC, Coagulation profile, Blood glucose, Cardiac enzymes, Lipid profile | Rule out: Transient ischemic attack, Hemorrhagic stroke, Hypoglycemia, Seizure, Migraine with aura\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"weakness\", \"vision\", \"loss\", \"weak\", \"Weakness\", \"Blurred Vision\", \"Numbness\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"CBC, Coagulation profile, Blood glucose, Cardiac enzymes, Lipid profile\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Warning signs present; Expected findings: Focal neurological deficits, Facial asymmetry, Hemiparesis, Dysarthria, Visual field defects\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Transient ischemic attack, Hemorrhagic stroke, Hypoglycemia, Seizure, Migraine with aura\"}, {\"urgency\": \"routine\", \"category\": \"endocrine\", \"icd_code\": \"E11\", \"severity\": \"moderate\", \"diagnosis\": \"Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus\", \"confidence\": 95, \"typical_onset\": \"gradual\", \"confidence_level\": \"High\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"Watch for: Diabetic ketoacidosis symptoms (fruity breath, confusion), Hypoglycemia, Severe dehydration | Consider tests: Fasting blood glucose >126 mg/dL, HbA1c >6.5%, OGTT, Lipid profile, Renal function tests | Rule out: Type 1 diabetes, Gestational diabetes, MODY, Secondary diabetes, Prediabetes\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"frequent urination\", \"fatigue\", \"weight loss\", \"thirst\", \"frequent\", \"urination\", \"blurred\", \"vision\", \"weight\", \"loss\", \"excessive\", \"skin\", \"fruity\", \"breath\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"Fasting blood glucose >126 mg/dL, HbA1c >6.5%, OGTT, Lipid profile, Renal function tests\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Warning signs present; Expected findings: May be obese, Acanthosis nigricans, Peripheral neuropathy signs, Retinopathy on fundoscopy\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Type 1 diabetes, Gestational diabetes, MODY, Secondary diabetes, Prediabetes\"}, {\"urgency\": \"routine\", \"category\": \"urological\", \"icd_code\": \"N39.0\", \"severity\": \"mild\", \"diagnosis\": \"Urinary Tract Infection\", \"confidence\": 95, \"typical_onset\": \"acute\", \"confidence_level\": \"High\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"Watch for: High fever with chills (suggests pyelonephritis), Flank pain, Nausea/vomiting, Altered mental status | Consider tests: Urinalysis (pyuria, bacteriuria, nitrites positive), Urine culture, CBC if systemic | Rule out: Vaginitis, STIs, Interstitial cystitis, Kidney stones, Prostatitis\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"frequent urination\", \"frequent\", \"urination\", \"Frequent Urination\", \"Painful Urination\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"Urinalysis (pyuria, bacteriuria, nitrites positive), Urine culture, CBC if systemic\", \"supporting_findings\": \"Matches primary disease symptoms; Expected findings: Suprapubic tenderness, Costovertebral angle tenderness (if pyelonephritis), Fever\", \"differential_diagnosis\": \"Vaginitis, STIs, Interstitial cystitis, Kidney stones, Prostatitis\"}, {\"urgency\": \"emergency\", \"category\": \"cardiovascular\", \"icd_code\": \"I21\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"diagnosis\": \"Acute Myocardial Infarction\", \"confidence\": 83, \"typical_onset\": \"sudden\", \"confidence_level\": \"High\", \"notes_for_doctor\": \"⚠️ EMERGENCY: Requires immediate attention | Watch for: Severe persistent chest pain >20 min, Cold clammy skin, Severe breathlessness, Loss of consciousness | Consider tests: Troponin I/T (elevated), CK-MB (elevated), ECG changes (ST elevation, Q waves), BNP | Rule out: Angina pectoris, Pulmonary embolism, Aortic dissection, Pericarditis, GERD, Musculoskeletal pain\", \"matching_symptoms\": [\"fatigue\", \"loss\", \"eating\", \"skin\", \"breath\", \"Fatigue\", \"Shortness of Breath\"], \"recommended_tests\": \"Troponin I/T (elevated), CK-M